preConditionHook:
// EL: lowerTail = minlist(open, close) - low; upperTail = high - maxlist(open,
// close). Measured from the BODY edge so it is the right tail whichever way the
// bar closed. MinList/MaxList are ACCEPTED for tick-grid PRICE operands only
// (EL_FEATURES.md): the open and the close are raw prices, so they differ by exactly 0
// or by at least one tick -- 1e9-1e11x the 2.22e-12 relational tolerance -- and
// whichever comparison the reserved word carries cannot matter. The plain
// ternary stand-in is therefore exact, the same arrangement BarOverlapFraction
// and ConsecutiveBarsLittleOverlap use. (<algorithm> is not among the emitted
// includes, so no std::min/std::max.)
//
// Every comparison below is multiplied, never a ratio: EL raises a runtime
// divide-by-zero on a doji whose high = low. A zero-range bar has both
// tails 0, which passes the two caps and fails the minTailFraction floor only
// when that input is above 0 -- at 0 the bar passes, which is EL's own answer.
lowerTail = (open[0] < close[0] ? open[0] : close[0]) - low[0];
upperTail = high[0] - (open[0] > close[0] ? open[0] : close[0]);
barRange = high[0] - low[0];
